/E (footsteps is wasted. This project aims to tap into that unused potential. Here, the physical force exerted by human footsteps acts as the primary input to initiate energy generation. Every footstep becomes a source of renewable energy when integrated with the right technology. 2. Piezoelectric Sensor \(Mechanical to Electrical Energy Conversion\) Piezoelectric sensors form the heart of this system. These sensors are made of crystalline materials that generate an electrical charge when subjected to mechanical stress. When a person steps on the sensor, the applied pressure causes deformation, which is instantly converted into an alternating voltage. Though small in magnitude, this voltage is valuable because it represents clean and renewable energy directly harvested from human)
