/Title (JUMPER WIRE: - A jumper wire is a short, insulated electrical wire used to connect components in a circuit, especially on breadboards, development boards, and prototyping platforms. Jumper wires are essential for building and testing temporary circuits without soldering. They allow easy and flexible wiring between points on a breadboard or between a breadboard and external components like sensors, microcontrollers \(e.g., Arduino, Raspberry Pi\), or power supplies.)
/Dest [43 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3574 0 R
/Next 3570 0 R
>>
endobj
