/Title (BREADBOARD: - A breadboard is a tool for prototyping electronic circuits, consisting of a grid of holes into which components and wires are inserted. Internally, the holes are connected by metal strips that create electrical connections. the breadboard gets its name from the original practice of building electronic circuits on literal wooden boards used for cutting bread, before specialized prototyping boards were invented. Today, modern breadboards are made from insulated plastic and include horizontal and vertical rows to help users create logical, organized circuit layouts.)
/Dest [42 0 R /Fit]
